{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omnigent-ai/omnigent/issues/comments/6476897924","html_url":"https://github.com/omnigent-ai/omnigent/issues/12030#issuecomment-6476897924","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omnigent-ai/omnigent/issues/12030","id":6476897924,"node_id":"IC_kwDOS3jeo88AAAABgg2ehA","user":{"login":"Paraphern","id":297951147,"node_id":"U_kgDOEcJfqw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297951147?u=16224a7a11d7f972e045eb313f5a08b9edd47f7b&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern","html_url":"https://github.com/Paraphern","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-28T18:11:53Z","updated_at":"2026-10-28T18:11:53Z","author_association":"NONE","body":"The shape is right - `inherit: false, allow: [names]` per harness is the correct boundary for spawned workers - and the write-surface motivation is the strongest part of the report. One design note from the pinning side of this problem: **an allowlist entry is only as strong as the handle it keys on, and a bare name is the weakest handle an MCP server offers.** Two failure modes eat name-keyed allowlists in exactly your managed-config setting:\n\n1. A server updates under an allowed name (managed push, minor bump) and serves a different surface - new tools, widened params - while the allowlist entry keeps saying \"allowed\". Your workers re-acquire the email/calendar/Drive/Slack/SQL write surfaces the list was written to exclude, without any config change on your side. Field rate for this class: 218 silent contract changes across the npm MCP top, most inside minor bumps; at registry scale, ~45% of pinned remote servers served a different tool list within a month (public HISTOR count).\n2. A renamed or replaced upstream can re-enter through the name slot (the dead-names class: config references tool/server names that no longer exist - or worse, exist differently).\n\nCheap hardening at spawn time: let each `allow` entry carry the expected surface - a per-server fingerprint over the tool contracts (`{name, description, inputSchema}` per tool, name-sorted, SHA-256) captured when the entry is written. Verify at agent spawn: mismatch = hold that server out of the session and emit an event, instead of silently allowing the new surface. That keeps the perf win (fewer proxies) and makes the safety win durable against upstream movement. We built the pin/diff half standalone ([rugsnare](https://github.com/Paraphern/rugsnare), Apache-2.0, zero deps; `--forbid-tool` for the hard write-class refusals in worker contexts) - the fingerprint format is an open spec if Omnigent wants to emit it natively.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omnigent-ai/omnigent/issues/comments/6476897924/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"pin":null}